    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1989075803016208581",
      "url": "https://x.com/ConvoyofHope/status/1989075803016208581",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ConvoyofHope/status/1989075803016208581",
      "text": "🚨 More than 1.4 million people are displaced in the aftermath of Typhoon Fung-wong. 🚨\n\nOver the weekend, the super typhoon made landfall in the northern Philippines, bringing powerful winds, flooding, and landslides.\n\nThis disaster comes just days after another destructive storm, Typhoon Kalmaegi, lashed the central Philippines and Vietnam.\n\nPeople in the Philippines have faced one disaster after another — from powerful typhoons to devastating earthquakes. Communities are being pushed to their limits, and thousands of families are in desperate need of food, water, and shelter.\n\nWhen disasters strike — one after another — Convoy of Hope is there. And because of generous supporters like you, we can bring hope to families who desperately need it.\n\nLearn more: https://t.co/zrAMRwFcoB\n\n(Photo by @AP)\n\n#typhoonfungwong #typhoonkalmaegi #philippines #disasterresponse",
